## 4. Entity Framework Core - Navigation Properties

### Critical Pattern: Explicit `.Include()`

```csharp
// ❌ WRONG: Navigation properties will be NULL
var products = _context.Products
    .Where(p => p.ShowOnHomePage)
    .ToList();
// products[0].ProductPictures == NULL ❌

// ✅ CORRECT: Explicitly include related data
var products = _context.Products
    .Include(p => p.ProductPictures)  // Load pictures
    .Where(p => p.ShowOnHomePage)
    .ToList();
// products[0].ProductPictures loaded ✅
```

**Action:** Before querying entities with relationships, check what navigation properties the view needs and add `.Include()` for each.

**Common includes for UI:**
- Products: `.Include(p => p.ProductPictures)`
- Categories: Category has `PictureId` directly (no include needed)
- Orders: `.Include(o => o.OrderItems).ThenInclude(oi => oi.Product)`

