## 5. Image Handling in nopCommerce

### How Pictures Work
1. **Storage:** Binary data in `Picture` table (database)
2. **Extraction:** `PictureService` writes to disk on first request
3. **Location:** `Nop.Web\content\images\thumbs\` (NOT `wwwroot\`)
4. **Naming:** `0000020_product-slug_300.jpeg` (PictureId_SeoFilename_Size)
5. **Auto-resize:** Service generates thumbs at requested size (e.g., 300px)

### Picture Loading Pattern
```csharp
// In Controller
private string GetProductPictureUrl(Product product)
{
    var pictures = product.ProductPictures?.OrderBy(x => x.DisplayOrder).ToList();
    
    if (pictures != null && pictures.Any())
    {
        return _pictureService.GetPictureUrl(pictures.First().PictureId, targetSize: 300);
    }
    
    return _pictureService.GetDefaultPictureUrl(targetSize: 300);
}

// In View
<img src="@ViewBag.PictureUrls[product.Id]" alt="@product.Name" />
```

### URL Pathing Fix
```csharp
// ❌ WRONG: Creates double slash http://localhost:5000//content/images/
var url = storeLocation + "/content/images/thumbs/" + fileName;

// ✅ CORRECT: Trim trailing slash first
var url = storeLocation.TrimEnd('/') + "/content/images/thumbs/" + fileName;
```

