## 6. HTML Structure Preservation

### Critical Rule: Match Legacy CSS Structure Exactly

Legacy `styles.css` expects specific HTML hierarchy. **DO NOT CHANGE** the structure:

```html
<!-- ✅ CORRECT: Legacy structure -->
<div class="product-grid home-page-product-grid">
    <div class="item-grid">
        <div class="item-box">
            <div class="product-item">
                <div class="picture">
                    <a href="/product-url">
                        <img src="/content/images/..." alt="Product" />
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div class="details">
                    <h2 class="product-title">
                        <a href="/product-url">Product Name</a>
                    </h2>
                    <div class="prices">
                        <span class="price actual-price">$1,200.00</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="buttons">
                    <input type="button" value="Add to cart" class="button-1 add-to-cart-button" />
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
```

**Before changing HTML:**
1. Read the legacy view from `nopCommerce-release-3.90` or `nopCommerce-release-4.70.0`
2. Identify the exact class structure
3. Preserve it in .NET 8.0 version
4. Test that styles apply correctly

