## 8. Debugging and Logging Strategy

### Mandatory Logging for UI Pages

```csharp
public ActionResult Index()
{
    // ✅ Log entry point
    _logger.LogDebug("HomeController.Index: Fetching homepage data from database");
    
    var products = _productService.GetAllProductsDisplayedOnHomePage();
    
    // ✅ Log data counts
    _logger.LogInformation("Fetched {ProductCount} products for homepage", products?.Count ?? 0);
    
    foreach (var product in products)
    {
        // ✅ Log critical data (pictures)
        var pictureCount = product.ProductPictures?.Count ?? 0;
        _logger.LogDebug("Product '{Name}' (ID: {Id}) has {Count} pictures", 
            product.Name, product.Id, pictureCount);
        
        if (pictureCount == 0)
        {
            // ✅ Log warnings for missing data
            _logger.LogWarning("Product '{Name}' has NO pictures - using default", product.Name);
        }
    }
    
    return View(products);
}
```

**Why this matters:** Logs reveal silent failures (missing pictures, null navigation properties, incorrect queries).

