## 9. CSS Modifications - When Allowed

### Acceptable Changes ✅
- Background colors: `body { background-color: #f5f8fa; }`
- Minor spacing adjustments to match legacy exactly
- Fixing broken responsive breakpoints (if responsive is in scope)

### Unacceptable Changes ❌
- Introducing new CSS frameworks (Bootstrap 5, Tailwind, etc.)
- Changing layout structure (grid → flexbox conversion)
- Adding utility classes not in legacy styles.css
- Inline styles in Razor views

**Rule:** If a style doesn't exist in legacy `styles.css`, ask user before adding it.

---

## 10. Testing Checklist for UI Pages

Before marking a page "complete," verify:

- [ ] **Data Loading:** All content from database (no hardcoded text/links)
- [ ] **Images:** Real images from DB (check file sizes: 30-300KB, not 2-3KB placeholders)
- [ ] **HTML Structure:** Matches legacy class hierarchy exactly
- [ ] **CSS Applied:** Styles render correctly (compare to legacy screenshot)
- [ ] **Navigation:** Links work (even if target pages not yet migrated)
- [ ] **Logging:** Debug logs show data flow clearly
- [ ] **No Errors:** Browser console has no JS errors, server logs clean
- [ ] **Visual Match:** Side-by-side comparison with legacy looks nearly identical

