## 11. Step-by-Step Migration Workflow

### For Each New Page:

```
1. STUDY LEGACY
   - Open nopCommerce-release-3.90 or 4.70.0
   - Read Controller, View, and any partial views
   - Take screenshot of legacy page for comparison

2. IDENTIFY DEPENDENCIES
   - What services does controller need? (Product, Category, Picture, etc.)
   - What navigation properties does view access?
   - Are there widgets or plugins involved?

3. UPDATE CONTROLLER
   - Add service dependencies via constructor DI
   - Write methods to fetch data from database
   - Use .Include() for navigation properties
   - Store supplementary data in ViewBag
   - Add debug logging

4. UPDATE VIEW
   - Replace @Html.Action() with @Html.PartialAsync()
   - Remove Request.Browser and obsolete code
   - Preserve exact HTML structure and CSS classes
   - Render data dynamically (foreach loops over DB data)
   - Add picture URLs from ViewBag

5. TEST INCREMENTALLY
   - Build and run application
   - Check logs for data loading
   - Verify images are real (check file sizes)
   - Compare to legacy screenshot
   - Test in browser, check console for errors

6. COMMIT
   - Write clear commit message with before/after
   - Reference specific fixes (EF Include, Html.Action replacement, etc.)
   - Note any remaining issues or TODOs

7. MOVE TO NEXT PAGE
   - Don't attempt multiple pages at once
   - Complete one page fully before starting another
```

---

## 12. Common Pitfalls and Solutions

| Problem | Cause | Solution |
|---------|-------|----------|
| Blank page rendering | `@Html.Action()` failed silently | Replace with `@Html.PartialAsync()` |
| "No Image" placeholders | Navigation property not loaded | Add `.Include(p => p.ProductPictures)` |
| Styles not applying | HTML structure changed | Restore legacy class hierarchy |
| 404 on images | Wrong path (wwwroot vs project root) | Images are in `content/images/`, not `wwwroot/content/` |
| Double slash in URLs | Didn't trim trailing slash | Use `storeLocation.TrimEnd('/')` |
| Runtime error on `.Count` | Dynamic type in view | Use strongly-typed model |
| Hardcoded product names | "Testing" with fake data | Always query database |

