## 14. When to Deviate from This Protocol

**Ask user permission before:**
- Changing HTML structure significantly
- Adding new CSS frameworks or libraries
- Skipping database loading in favor of hardcoded data
- Making responsive layout changes
- Modifying admin area (out of current scope)

**Don't ask, just do:**
- Fixing `@Html.Action()` to `@Html.PartialAsync()`
- Adding `.Include()` for navigation properties
- Trimming trailing slashes in URL construction
- Adding debug logging
- Removing obsolete `Request.Browser` code

---

## 15. Success Criteria

A page migration is **COMPLETE** when:

1. ✅ Visual appearance matches legacy (pixel-perfect or very close)
2. ✅ All data loads from database dynamically
3. ✅ Images are real (30-300KB file sizes)
4. ✅ HTML structure preserves legacy CSS class hierarchy
5. ✅ No console errors, no server errors
6. ✅ Debug logs show clear data flow
7. ✅ Code committed with clear before/after description
8. ✅ User confirms "looks good, move on"

---

**This protocol is based on proven patterns from successful homepage migration. Apply consistently to all UI pages.**
